## Why This Is Asked

Evaluate ability to implement host integrity controls with minimal downtime using native RH tooling, idempotence, and rollback.

## Key Concepts

- rpm -V usage for binary integrity
- systemd service and timer
- Baseline diffing and logging
- Alerting and rollback strategy
- Reinstall path from diffs

## Code Example

```javascript
const { execSync } = require('child_process');
const fs = require('fs');
const baseline = '/var/log/integrity/baseline.txt';
const current = execSync('rpm -V -a').toString();
const base = fs.readFileSync(baseline, 'utf8');
const nl = String.fromCharCode(10);
const diff = current.split(/\\r?\\n/).filter(l => !base.includes(l)).join(nl);
if (diff) {
  fs.appendFileSync('/var/log/sys_integrity.log', diff + nl);
  console.log('ALERT');
} else {
  console.log('OK');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adapt this for multi-host environments and centralize reporting?
- How would you minimize false positives around legitimate upgrades?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to build a multi-tenant TLS termination with live updates in a containerized RH9 setup, including security and networking constraints.

## Key Concepts
- TLS with SNI and per-tenant certs
- Podman container networking
- Local CA management and cert rotation
- systemd-based zero-downtime reloads
- SELinux policy and nftables isolation
- End-to-end test planning

## Code Example
```javascript
// watcher: rotate tenant certs and reload proxy
const fs = require('fs');
const { execSync } = require('child_process');
const watchDir = '/var/lib/proxy/certs';
const watcher = require('chokidar').watch(watchDir);
watcher.on('change', (path) => {
  if (path.endsWith('.pem')) {
    fs.copyFileSync(`${watchDir}/current.pem`, '/var/run/proxy/current.pem.bak');
    execSync('systemctl reload rhproxy');
  }
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you revoke a tenant cert without downtime?
- How would you validate multi-tenant isolation under load?
